POOL = 16
ITEMS = [
    ('An SSL/SSH inspection profile set to certificate inspection can read which part of an HTTPS session?',
     ['Server name and certificate', 'The full URL and query string', 'The files being downloaded', 'The HTTP request headers'],
     'A',
     'Certificate inspection reads only the SNI and the server certificate, so it can rate a site by domain. The URL path, headers and file content stay encrypted unless full inspection decrypts the session.'),
    ('Which inspection lets antivirus scan a file downloaded over HTTPS?',
     ['Certificate inspection', 'Full SSL inspection', 'SNI inspection only', 'No inspection profile'],
     'B',
     'Antivirus needs the decrypted payload, and only full (deep) inspection decrypts the session. Certificate inspection never sees the file content.'),
    ('Users see a certificate warning on every HTTPS site after full SSL inspection is enabled. What is the usual fix?',
     ['Switch the policy to flow-based mode', 'Disable the SNI check in the profile', 'Trust the FortiGate CA on clients', 'Exempt every web category'],
     'C',
     'In full inspection FortiGate re-signs each server certificate with its own CA, such as Fortinet_CA_SSL. Clients trust the re-signed certificate only once that CA is in their trusted root store.'),
    ('Which certificate does FortiGate use by default to re-sign server certificates in full SSL inspection?',
     ['Fortinet_Factory', 'Fortinet_SSL', 'Fortinet_Wifi', 'Fortinet_CA_SSL'],
     'D',
     'Fortinet_CA_SSL is the default CA for deep inspection; each FortiGate generates its own. Fortinet_Factory and Fortinet_SSL are server certificates, not signing CAs.'),
    ('With full SSL inspection on, a server presents an expired certificate. What controls the action FortiGate takes?',
     ['The expired certificate setting', 'The IPS sensor signature action', 'The web filter category action', "The antivirus profile's scan action"],
     'A',
     "The inspection profile's invalid certificate settings include an action for expired server certificates: allow, block, or pass with an untrusted re-signed certificate so the browser warns. Untrusted, revoked and validation-failed certificates have their own actions. Web filter and IPS do not judge certificates."),
    ('Why are banking and health care categories exempt in the default deep-inspection profile?',
     ['Their sites never carry malware', 'Privacy and compliance rules', 'FortiGuard cannot rate them', 'They always use pinned keys'],
     'B',
     'Decrypting financial and medical traffic can breach privacy rules, so the default profile exempts those categories. Exemption is a policy choice, not a claim that the sites are safe.'),
    ('A mobile banking app fails only when full SSL inspection is applied. What is the most likely cause?',
     ['The app uses QUIC by default', "IPS blocked the app's signature", 'The app pins its certificate', 'The DNS filter rated it as spam'],
     'C',
     "Certificate pinning makes the app accept only its own server certificate, so FortiGate's re-signed one is rejected. Exempting that destination from inspection is the usual fix."),
    ('Where can you exempt a specific server address from full SSL inspection?',
     ['In the IPS sensor for the policy', 'In the static URL filter list', 'In the firewall address group', 'In the SSL inspection profile'],
     'D',
     'The inspection profile has exemption lists for addresses, FortiGuard categories and reputable websites. A static URL filter controls web filtering, not decryption.'),
    ('A web server listens for HTTPS on TCP 8443. How do you make full inspection decrypt it?',
     ['List 8443 as an HTTPS port', 'Create a VIP mapping 8443 to 443', 'Add 8443 to the IPS sensor', 'Enable SNI check on port 443'],
     'A',
     'The inspection profile lists the ports treated as each protocol, so adding 8443 under HTTPS makes FortiGate decrypt it. The profile can also inspect all ports.'),
    ("In certificate inspection, what happens when the SNI does not match the certificate's CN or SAN and SNI check is set to strict?",
     ['FortiGate rates by the CN instead', 'The session is blocked', 'The SNI is used for rating', 'FortiGate switches to full inspection'],
     'B',
     "Strict SNI check blocks a session whose SNI does not match the certificate, a sign of domain fronting. With the check enabled but not strict, FortiGate uses the certificate's CN for rating."),
    ('A site using HSTS shows an error the browser will not let users bypass under full inspection. What is missing?',
     ['A web filter override', 'Flow-based inspection', 'Trust for the FortiGate CA', 'A matching DNS filter entry'],
     'C',
     'HSTS removes the option to click past certificate errors, so an untrusted re-signing CA leaves the site unreachable. Installing the FortiGate CA on clients lets the re-signed certificate validate.'),
    ('Which inspection mode buffers the whole file before scanning and can replace a blocked page with a replacement message?',
     ['Flow-based with certificate inspection', 'Flow-based with quick scan', 'Flow-based with full inspection', 'Proxy-based inspection'],
     'D',
     'Proxy-based inspection buffers files and rebuilds sessions, which allows full replacement messages and more features. Flow-based inspection scans packets as they pass, using fewer resources.'),
    ('Which security profile behavior needs proxy-based inspection on the policy?',
     ['Buffering whole files before scanning', 'Application control signatures', 'FortiGuard category web filtering', 'IPS signature matching'],
     'A',
     'Buffering complete files and rebuilding the session is a proxy-based feature. Flow-based inspection scans packets as they pass and still supports application control, FortiGuard web filtering and IPS.'),
    ('Full SSL inspection is applied to inbound traffic for a company web server. What should the profile use?',
     ['The Fortinet_CA_SSL certificate', 'Protect SSL server mode', 'Certificate inspection only', 'The untrusted CA certificate'],
     'B',
     "For inbound inspection the profile protects an SSL server and uses that server's own certificate and key, so external clients see no warning. Re-signing with the FortiGate CA suits outbound traffic only."),
    ('A web filter blocks a site by category even though only certificate inspection is applied. How was the site rated?',
     ['By the full URL path', 'By keywords on the page', 'By the SNI or certificate', 'By the downloaded file type'],
     'C',
     'With certificate inspection, FortiGuard rates the domain taken from the SNI or the certificate, so category blocking still works. Keyword and file type filters need the decrypted content.'),
    ('Which statement about certificate inspection is true?',
     ['It needs the FortiGate CA on clients', 'It decrypts and re-encrypts traffic', 'It blocks pinned applications', 'It causes no certificate warnings'],
     'D',
     'Certificate inspection does not decrypt or re-sign, so browsers see the real server certificate and raise no warnings. Installing the FortiGate CA matters only for full inspection.'),
] 
assert len(ITEMS) == POOL
for i, it in enumerate(ITEMS):
    assert it[2] == "ABCD"[i % 4], (i, it[2])
    assert len(it[1]) == 4 and len(set(it[1])) == 4, i
